  "id": "masson-disk",
  "term": "Masson disk",
  "definition": "A Masson disk is a laboratory device used in early psychology to study fluctuations of visual attention. It is a rotating white disk marked with a segmented black line that produces concentric grey rings, allowing the observer to note the alternating appearance and disappearance of an outer ring over time.",
